# Copy to .env and adjust. Nothing secret belongs here: API keys (AI provider, Kaggle server,
# decision model, email) are pasted into the app's Settings screen and stored locally.
#
# scripts/start.sh sources this file before launching anything. Plain KEY=VALUE lines only.

# Ports. APP_PORT is the address you open in the browser (the agent: chat, and the web UI it forwards
# from the API); the API, which renders the web UI, runs behind it on API_INTERNAL_PORT.
APP_PORT=8000
API_INTERNAL_PORT=8010

# Separate instances need distinct ports and a distinct run directory.
#AGENT_HIRE_RUN_DIR=.run/second

# Where the app keeps your profile, documents and generated résumés.
# Default (Linux): ~/.local/share/Agent-Hire
#AGENT_HIRE_DATA_DIR=/media/you/big-disk/Agent-Hire

# Chats, schedules and uploads of the agent. Default: ~/.local/share/Agent-Hire/agent
#AGENT_HIRE_AGENT_DIR=

# The scraped job index (SQLite, ~1.5 GB for ~230k jobs). Default: <app data dir>/jobs.
# Keep it on a native Linux filesystem: on NTFS/FUSE drives SQLite is ~3x slower.
#AGENT_HIRE_JOBS_DIR=
# Temporary scrape output (raw responses, deleted after each run is imported). A full pass can
# use several GB while it runs, so a bigger drive is fine here. Default: <jobs dir>/runs.
#AGENT_HIRE_SCRAPE_RUNS_DIR=
# Companies scraped in parallel during a run.
#AGENT_HIRE_SCRAPE_CONCURRENCY=4

# Generated on first start into the run directory; set it yourself only when running the API and
# the agent by hand (`make api` + `make agent`), with the same value for both.
#AGENT_HIRE_AGENT_SECRET=
